(6149869, 905726, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This is the first image to pop up for me in voting - excellent!! Love the colours here - especially the polaroid blue hues. I like how it feels like a scratched transparency. I can clearly see the flower petals but I''m delighted you''ve retained so much mystery in this image. I like how it offer low and high contrast at the same time - I''m not sure how you''ve pulled that off.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: I really hope others enjoy this as much as I do. I wonder if the parallel Nixter challenge will open people up a little to the less conventional images sometimes offered up?</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This is the first image to pop up for me in voting - excellent!! Love the colours here - especially the polaroid blue hues. I like how it feels like a scratched transparency. I can clearly see the flower petals but I''m delighted you''ve retained so much mystery in this image. I like how it offer low and high contrast at the same time - I''m not sure how you''ve pulled that off. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: I really hope others enjoy this as much as I do. I wonder if the parallel Nixter challenge will open people up a little to the less conventional images sometimes offered up?', '2010-09-02 15:14:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6149870, 906566, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is a very beautiful image. The boldness of the aspect ratio works perfectly.</td>', 'This is a very beautiful image. The boldness of the aspect ratio works perfectly.', '2010-09-02 15:16:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6149872, 906829, 100393, '<td valign="top">Beautifully done.</td>', 'Beautifully done.', '2010-09-02 15:17:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6149877, 906389, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: What a quirky scene! The looks on both of their faces when put together makes for amazing story telling. The composition is really clever, with the eye drawn to the background and the negative space above, it has the feel of a comic cell await lettering - the juxtaposition of (non-speech) balloons adds to the overall mental image. The tilt to the table is masterful too and reinforces the visual effect and crafted feel. The high contrast black and white handling - fabulous choice!<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Quite fabulous - i''m sure this will pick up a lot of admirers.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: What a quirky scene! The looks on both of their faces when put together makes for amazing story telling. The composition is really clever, with the eye drawn to the background and the negative space above, it has the feel of a comic cell await lettering - the juxtaposition of (non-speech) balloons adds to the overall mental image. The tilt to the table is masterful too and reinforces the visual effect and crafted feel. The high contrast black and white handling - fabulous choice! Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: Quite fabulous - i''m sure this will pick up a lot of admirers.', '2010-09-02 15:22:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6149892, 906871, 96751, '<td valign="top">So sweet.  A bit oversharpened in the chest area.</td>', 'So sweet.  A bit oversharpened in the chest area.', '2010-09-02 15:40:41.000000', NULL, 1),
