(6151718, 905958, 23484, '<td valign="top">Great shot. Perfectly cropped and composed.9</td>', 'Great shot. Perfectly cropped and composed.9', '2010-09-04 09:05:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(6151719, 906679, 23484, '<td valign="top">Nice job on the lighting.</td>', 'Nice job on the lighting.', '2010-09-04 09:07:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6151721, 906846, 23484, '<td valign="top">The clouds give this such an ominous feel.</td>', 'The clouds give this such an ominous feel.', '2010-09-04 09:07:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6151722, 906562, 23484, '<td valign="top">Neat shot. Kind of abstract.</td>', 'Neat shot. Kind of abstract.', '2010-09-04 09:08:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(6151723, 902167, 23484, '<td valign="top">Looks like a little girl in a war torn country. Nice high contrast B&amp;W.</td>', 'Looks like a little girl in a war torn country. Nice high contrast B&W.', '2010-09-04 09:09:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6151724, 905999, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very nice pose and processing.</td>', 'Very nice pose and processing.', '2010-09-04 09:09:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6151725, 904471, 23484, '<td valign="top">I like the glowing tracks.</td>', 'I like the glowing tracks.', '2010-09-04 09:10:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6151726, 904201, 23484, '<td valign="top">I see you. Excellent.</td>', 'I see you. Excellent.', '2010-09-04 09:12:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6151727, 906478, 23484, '<td valign="top">I like the lower saturation for this.</td>', 'I like the lower saturation for this.', '2010-09-04 09:12:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6151751, 905721, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: There are a number of features of this image that I like - the slightly tone-mapped look suits that suits the image; the story behind the girl and the shop - we wonder if she works there or at the adjacent property - we wonder what she makes of you as you take the shot. I like the overall composition too - where you have placed the various elements within your frame.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much - the deep shadow on her face means we don''t have eye-contact. I''m not sure if that would improve the image any but it would certainly be different.<br/> <br/>Overall: A great offering.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: There are a number of features of this image that I like - the slightly tone-mapped look suits that suits the image; the story behind the girl and the shop - we wonder if she works there or at the adjacent property - we wonder what she makes of you as you take the shot. I like the overall composition too - where you have placed the various elements within your frame. Critical stuff: Not much - the deep shadow on her face means we don''t have eye-contact. I''m not sure if that would improve the image any but it would certainly be different. Overall: A great offering.', '2010-09-04 09:59:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6151753, 906705, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: A dying breed - in more ways than one! What an interesting composition - the juxtaposition between the foreground and background subjects is as stark as it is effective - I really like that. I like the colours of the bus too and the overall golden lighting hue.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The foreground  hand - without it I think the image would have much more mystery; it would make me think more about where you were in relation to the subject what you took the shot.<br/> <br/>Overall: A very effective image.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: A dying breed - in more ways than one! What an interesting composition - the juxtaposition between the foreground and background subjects is as stark as it is effective - I really like that. I like the colours of the bus too and the overall golden lighting hue. Critical stuff: The foreground  hand - without it I think the image would have much more mystery; it would make me think more about where you were in relation to the subject what you took the shot. Overall: A very effective image.', '2010-09-04 10:06:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6151754, 906352, 100393, '<td valign="top">A fine model portrait but the background kills it for me a bit.</td>', 'A fine model portrait but the background kills it for me a bit.', '2010-09-04 10:07:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6151756, 906705, 91496, '<td valign="top">Nice effect with the blurred out man.  Not sure it really goes with the background though.  They do not seem to compliment each other or really tell a story.  I do not like these letterox borders.  In this case the border  stands out here as much as the photo.</td>', 'Nice effect with the blurred out man.  Not sure it really goes with the background though.  They do not seem to compliment each other or really tell a story.  I do not like these letterox borders.  In this case the border  stands out here as much as the photo.', '2010-09-04 10:10:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6151758, 906683, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: A slightly bizarre image but an effective one. It very much has a crafted feel about it - it feels deliberate in a way that goes beyond ''staged'' - as much of a planned moment as a planned photo. The composition is clinical in its precision and the capture has timing to match. The high contrast look suits the scene perfectly.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''m never a fan of crunchy foliage but I''m not sure diffusing it would''ve yielded an image with the same impact.<br/> <br/>Overall: Demonstrates mastery - I''m looking forward to finding out who made this.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: A slightly bizarre image but an effective one. It very much has a crafted feel about it - it feels deliberate in a way that goes beyond ''staged'' - as much of a planned moment as a planned photo. The composition is clinical in its precision and the capture has timing to match. The high contrast look suits the scene perfectly. Critical stuff: I''m never a fan of crunchy foliage but I''m not sure diffusing it would''ve yielded an image with the same impact. Overall: Demonstrates mastery - I''m looking forward to finding out who made this.', '2010-09-04 10:13:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6151764, 906562, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I really like this - the colour palette stop me in my tracks - one of those picture that reminds us to lift our head and look around more often. The swathes of black negative space hurt the image not at all and serve to further emphasise the mood of the room.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: A scene like this only has a finite amount of interest in it and even when captured very nicely, the upper limit of interest is less than in images with a stronger story to tell.<br/> <br/>Overall: I do like it. Nicely made.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I really like this - the colour palette stop me in my tracks - one of those picture that reminds us to lift our head and look around more often. The swathes of black negative space hurt the image not at all and serve to further emphasise the mood of the room. Critical stuff: A scene like this only has a finite amount of interest in it and even when captured very nicely, the upper limit of interest is less than in images with a stronger story to tell. Overall: I do like it. Nicely made.', '2010-09-04 10:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
