(6152375, 906366, 110250, '<td valign="top">Absolutely LOVE the colors, composition and detail of this shot. I''m giving it a 10.  Couldn''t improve in any way. WELL DONE!</td>', 'Absolutely LOVE the colors, composition and detail of this shot. I''m giving it a 10.  Couldn''t improve in any way. WELL DONE!', '2010-09-05 08:29:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152388, 906750, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Wonderfully made. I know the back story to this image which makes it all the more poignant, but even when putting that to one side, this was always likely to hit my sweet spot. The combination of elements in this image - the doll head, the inserted hands and the vertical hair tuft all make for a most intriguing image and the use of a Lensbaby complements the composition perfectly.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much, but a few personal taste things - I do think a tad more space at the bottom may have worked a little better - the lack of edge burning on that side (paradoxically) emphasises the asymmetry. I also think the image could have stood slightly more contrast.<br/> <br/>Overall: A wonderfully creative piece.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Wonderfully made. I know the back story to this image which makes it all the more poignant, but even when putting that to one side, this was always likely to hit my sweet spot. The combination of elements in this image - the doll head, the inserted hands and the vertical hair tuft all make for a most intriguing image and the use of a Lensbaby complements the composition perfectly. Critical stuff: Not much, but a few personal taste things - I do think a tad more space at the bottom may have worked a little better - the lack of edge burning on that side (paradoxically) emphasises the asymmetry. I also think the image could have stood slightly more contrast. Overall: A wonderfully creative piece.', '2010-09-05 10:22:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152389, 906790, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Great use of blur (Lensbaby?) - I really like the grain and coloration too; the choices you have made make the viewer become more aware and thus to consider more the lighting and texture of your subject.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Your editing and shooting choices have brought much interest to an otherwise low interest scene.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Great use of blur (Lensbaby?) - I really like the grain and coloration too; the choices you have made make the viewer become more aware and thus to consider more the lighting and texture of your subject. Critical stuff: Not much at all. Overall: Your editing and shooting choices have brought much interest to an otherwise low interest scene.', '2010-09-05 10:27:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152391, 906572, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I like what you''ve tried to do here - using the motion blur to emphasise the linearity of the tree trunks. The dappled lighting serves to add some depth to the image too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: As sound as your vision is, I don''t think you''ve pulled it off. The large mass of ground that makes up the lower half of the image isn''t (in my view) particularly suited to that sort of effect and the trees themselves are not vertical enough for the technique to work.<br/> <br/>Overall: I like this sort of image but this one doesn''t do it for me I''m afraid.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I like what you''ve tried to do here - using the motion blur to emphasise the linearity of the tree trunks. The dappled lighting serves to add some depth to the image too. Critical stuff: As sound as your vision is, I don''t think you''ve pulled it off. The large mass of ground that makes up the lower half of the image isn''t (in my view) particularly suited to that sort of effect and the trees themselves are not vertical enough for the technique to work. Overall: I like this sort of image but this one doesn''t do it for me I''m afraid.', '2010-09-05 10:38:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152392, 905057, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is a very pretty image - has an <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=69668" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">njsabs</a> feel about it.</td>', 'This is a very pretty image - has an  njsabs feel about it.', '2010-09-05 10:39:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152397, 906594, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: A nice street scene to capture here and I admire your eye to have seen and captured it. The two characters complement each other very well.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: There is quite a lot here which makes the image sub-optimal (at least to my eyes): The cluttered background - the cars kill the image; making this a square crop, cropping left of the Peugeot would have made the image a lot better. The image needs to be brighter, a little more contrast with some highlight recovery done afterwards to prevent subsequent blowing of highlights. The rectangular vignette is horrible - far too prominent; if you are going to use them, I think elliptical are far more effective and smoother transitions than this are required for them to remain subtle.<br/> <br/>Overall: A nearly image, but too much conflicts with my view of how such an image should be edited. (A 5, but could be a lot more).</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: A nice street scene to capture here and I admire your eye to have seen and captured it. The two characters complement each other very well. Critical stuff: There is quite a lot here which makes the image sub-optimal (at least to my eyes): The cluttered background - the cars kill the image; making this a square crop, cropping left of the Peugeot would have made the image a lot better. The image needs to be brighter, a little more contrast with some highlight recovery done afterwards to prevent subsequent blowing of highlights. The rectangular vignette is horrible - far too prominent; if you are going to use them, I think elliptical are far more effective and smoother transitions than this are required for them to remain subtle. Overall: A nearly image, but too much conflicts with my view of how such an image should be edited. (A 5, but could be a lot more).', '2010-09-05 10:47:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152415, 906141, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I feel ambushed by this image - but in a good way! Spectacular processing elevates this image above mainstream floral work; the coloration, the texture and particularly the gradation of tones distinguish this image.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: tremendous stuff - I''d love to know your processing steps.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I feel ambushed by this image - but in a good way! Spectacular processing elevates this image above mainstream floral work; the coloration, the texture and particularly the gradation of tones distinguish this image. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: tremendous stuff - I''d love to know your processing steps.', '2010-09-05 11:12:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152418, 906379, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I like unusual portraits and this falls squarely into that camp. The hemi-face coupled with the deep perspective offered by the industrial background works really well. I think your choice of aperture offers a DOF that works really well. The aspect ratio / crop is just perfect for this<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: There are some minor things that bother me. The blue fringing in the background, the blown highlights top right, the slightly jaundiced appearance of the skin tone - but all of these are only slightly sub-optimal.<br/> <br/>Overall. Very nice work</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I like unusual portraits and this falls squarely into that camp. The hemi-face coupled with the deep perspective offered by the industrial background works really well. I think your choice of aperture offers a DOF that works really well. The aspect ratio / crop is just perfect for this Critical stuff: There are some minor things that bother me. The blue fringing in the background, the blown highlights top right, the slightly jaundiced appearance of the skin tone - but all of these are only slightly sub-optimal. Overall. Very nice work', '2010-09-05 11:17:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152419, 906888, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: There are lots of elements I like about this image - but most of all I like the POV. The curvature of the glass tricks the eye into think there is some distortion of reality here. The reflected sky binds the image together very effectively.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much - the lower part of the street light could''ve shown a little bit of texture.<br/> <br/>Overall: A very nice architectural shot.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: There are lots of elements I like about this image - but most of all I like the POV. The curvature of the glass tricks the eye into think there is some distortion of reality here. The reflected sky binds the image together very effectively. Critical stuff: Not much - the lower part of the street light could''ve shown a little bit of texture. Overall: A very nice architectural shot.', '2010-09-05 11:22:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152420, 906638, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is beautifully done - difficult to get this level of crispness but to avoid ugly crunchy foliage.</td>', 'This is beautifully done - difficult to get this level of crispness but to avoid ugly crunchy foliage.', '2010-09-05 11:23:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152421, 906792, 76335, '<td valign="top">Extra points for not just photographing the bridge. I like the human element here.</td>', 'Extra points for not just photographing the bridge. I like the human element here.', '2010-09-05 11:25:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152422, 906453, 76335, '<td valign="top">Fabulous framing, DOF, tones...</td>', 'Fabulous framing, DOF, tones...', '2010-09-05 11:25:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152424, 906332, 76335, '<td valign="top">I like that it''s casual, though the shadow running through her eye is a bit distracting.</td>', 'I like that it''s casual, though the shadow running through her eye is a bit distracting.', '2010-09-05 11:26:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152425, 906684, 76335, '<td valign="top">I can''t resist those late day shadows either. Looks fun!</td>', 'I can''t resist those late day shadows either. Looks fun!', '2010-09-05 11:27:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152426, 904239, 100393, '<td valign="top">Super-fabulous lighting, great model, wonderful room, well processed too.<br/> <br/>I would never have been brave enough to use the background so prominently but it works so well.<br/> <br/>I know what great work this is but for me the slightly off-verticals bug the hell out of me and I wish it was just very slightly brighter.<br/> <br/>Great, great image though - much better than any of my model work.</td>', 'Super-fabulous lighting, great model, wonderful room, well processed too. I would never have been brave enough to use the background so prominently but it works so well. I know what great work this is but for me the slightly off-verticals bug the hell out of me and I wish it was just very slightly brighter. Great, great image though - much better than any of my model work.', '2010-09-05 11:28:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152427, 903952, 76335, '<td valign="top">Looks like the underside of some piece of exercise equipment -- a bench? Points for originality. (I see some chroma noise; might have worked better in black and white anyway.)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-09-08 20:38:15.</i></td>', 'Looks like the underside of some piece of exercise equipment -- a bench? Points for originality. (I see some chroma noise; might have worked better in black and white anyway.)', '2010-09-05 11:29:44.000000', '2010-09-08 21:38:15.000000', 1),
(6152428, 906814, 76335, '<td valign="top">At first glance, I thought it was snow. Chilling just the same, and a great archaeological find/capture.</td>', 'At first glance, I thought it was snow. Chilling just the same, and a great archaeological find/capture.', '2010-09-05 11:31:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152431, 906813, 76335, '<td valign="top">Feautibul.</td>', 'Feautibul.', '2010-09-05 11:32:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152432, 906430, 76335, '<td valign="top">Nice panorama, good rhythm in the reflections of the light culminating with the lighthouse.</td>', 'Nice panorama, good rhythm in the reflections of the light culminating with the lighthouse.', '2010-09-05 11:33:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152433, 906109, 76335, '<td valign="top">This had to be a challenging shot to get. Good job given everything working against you.</td>', 'This had to be a challenging shot to get. Good job given everything working against you.', '2010-09-05 11:34:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152435, 905958, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Such a bold composition - I love it. A perfect image for the ''Film Noir'' challenge we have never had - the aspect ratio suits the image perfectly. Superb use of negative space and the toning is marvellous too. A real story being told here.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: great image - simple, but so effective.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Such a bold composition - I love it. A perfect image for the ''Film Noir'' challenge we have never had - the aspect ratio suits the image perfectly. Superb use of negative space and the toning is marvellous too. A real story being told here. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: great image - simple, but so effective.', '2010-09-05 11:34:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152436, 906885, 76335, '<td valign="top">I love the bold colors and how you arranged (framed) your composition. I''ll find a seven in your score.</td>', 'I love the bold colors and how you arranged (framed) your composition. I''ll find a seven in your score.', '2010-09-05 11:35:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152437, 906606, 76335, '<td valign="top">Great angle/point of view. Feel like I''m out there.</td>', 'Great angle/point of view. Feel like I''m out there.', '2010-09-05 11:35:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152438, 906137, 76335, '<td valign="top">Eek! What''s the story here? Chilling...</td>', 'Eek! What''s the story here? Chilling...', '2010-09-05 11:36:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152439, 906888, 76335, '<td valign="top">Good contrast punctuates an already strong composition. Nice work.</td>', 'Good contrast punctuates an already strong composition. Nice work.', '2010-09-05 11:37:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152443, 906580, 76335, '<td valign="top">Focus seems to be on the rock more than the kitty kitty. <br/> <br/>Also, when photographing at the zoo, consider that just about every animal photo has been taken and posted to DPC.</td>', 'Focus seems to be on the rock more than the kitty kitty.  Also, when photographing at the zoo, consider that just about every animal photo has been taken and posted to DPC.', '2010-09-05 11:39:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152444, 904668, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''ve refused to be impressed by landscape images this month but how can I resist this one? The difference here is that I get the feeling of photographic involvement, not just the capturing of a scene. Your POV is so important in conveying a crafted feel - move your camera 1 foot in any direction and your image would be less effective. Your processing (is it HDR? if so, it certainly isn''t over-done) is really excellent.<br/> <br/>Optimised in a way many images aren''t. Impressive work.<br/> <br/>(By way of excusing my opening comment - I do appreciate that landscape work is hard - mine are useless; but nonetheless - few evoke a sense of the photographer as this one does).)</td>', 'I''ve refused to be impressed by landscape images this month but how can I resist this one? The difference here is that I get the feeling of photographic involvement, not just the capturing of a scene. Your POV is so important in conveying a crafted feel - move your camera 1 foot in any direction and your image would be less effective. Your processing (is it HDR? if so, it certainly isn''t over-done) is really excellent. Optimised in a way many images aren''t. Impressive work. (By way of excusing my opening comment - I do appreciate that landscape work is hard - mine are useless; but nonetheless - few evoke a sense of the photographer as this one does).)', '2010-09-05 11:39:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152445, 902037, 76335, '<td valign="top">Beautiful, the sharp petals against the watery backdrop.</td>', 'Beautiful, the sharp petals against the watery backdrop.', '2010-09-05 11:39:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152446, 906753, 76335, '<td valign="top">Nice pose. Smile and overall expression feel a little forced.</td>', 'Nice pose. Smile and overall expression feel a little forced.', '2010-09-05 11:40:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152448, 906431, 76335, '<td valign="top">A good subject -- the processing of the sky is a bit outlandish.</td>', 'A good subject -- the processing of the sky is a bit outlandish.', '2010-09-05 11:43:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152449, 906782, 76335, '<td valign="top">This might be the only insect macro of the challenge that moves me. Love how he surfaces from the blurry bokeh depths.</td>', 'This might be the only insect macro of the challenge that moves me. Love how he surfaces from the blurry bokeh depths.', '2010-09-05 11:44:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152450, 906631, 76335, '<td valign="top">Looks good in black and white. I like how the light is hitting them such that just their outlines are prominent.</td>', 'Looks good in black and white. I like how the light is hitting them such that just their outlines are prominent.', '2010-09-05 11:45:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152451, 906685, 76335, '<td valign="top">Fabulous double exposure effect. What an eye!</td>', 'Fabulous double exposure effect. What an eye!', '2010-09-05 11:46:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152467, 906790, 117831, '<td valign="top">This is kind of an odd image, but I really like the contract of colors and the cool textures. 7!</td>', 'This is kind of an odd image, but I really like the contract of colors and the cool textures. 7!', '2010-09-05 12:14:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152468, 906400, 117831, '<td valign="top">Bear? I love the rowboats, the color and random order about them are nice! 7!</td>', 'Bear? I love the rowboats, the color and random order about them are nice! 7!', '2010-09-05 12:14:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152471, 906548, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Excellent use of the reflection - coupled with the grain, it very much has a painting feel about it. The amplitude of the waves is perfect - it adds interest without obliterating the tree line.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The brownish area bottom left of the image is a little distracting - a crop or clone here may have been in order.<br/> <br/>Overall: Very nice image.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Excellent use of the reflection - coupled with the grain, it very much has a painting feel about it. The amplitude of the waves is perfect - it adds interest without obliterating the tree line. Critical stuff: The brownish area bottom left of the image is a little distracting - a crop or clone here may have been in order. Overall: Very nice image.', '2010-09-05 12:22:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152478, 906446, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: A caged bird is a brave subject to offer up but I like the honesty of this one; the prominence of the cage gives the capture an authenticity that serves the image well. The tone-mapping works perfectly too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing.<br/> <br/>Overall: Very well measured image.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: A caged bird is a brave subject to offer up but I like the honesty of this one; the prominence of the cage gives the capture an authenticity that serves the image well. The tone-mapping works perfectly too. Critical stuff: Nothing. Overall: Very well measured image.', '2010-09-05 12:28:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152481, 906306, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Lovely stuff - the gold coloration is very pretty indeed and the degree of motion blur is just right. The contrast of the reflected areas is wonderful, giving a really rich feel to the image.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing.<br/> <br/>Overall: I really like this - aside from the coloration, very Nixtery (always a good thing!)</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Lovely stuff - the gold coloration is very pretty indeed and the degree of motion blur is just right. The contrast of the reflected areas is wonderful, giving a really rich feel to the image. Critical stuff: Nothing. Overall: I really like this - aside from the coloration, very Nixtery (always a good thing!)', '2010-09-05 12:31:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152482, 902414, 116730, '<td valign="top">I really love this photo!</td>', 'I really love this photo!', '2010-09-05 12:31:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152483, 904442, 67258, '<td valign="top">The hint of rim lighting on your subjects really move this up a notch - you have captured/created a lovely atmosphere.</td>', 'The hint of rim lighting on your subjects really move this up a notch - you have captured/created a lovely atmosphere.', '2010-09-05 12:31:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152488, 904668, 116730, '<td valign="top">I love the clarity</td>', 'I love the clarity', '2010-09-05 12:34:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152489, 905733, 67258, '<td valign="top">I normally dislike selective desaturation, but here it works; it has a purpose, and is integral to the concept. An intriguing image that holds my attention and cries out for repeated viewings.</td>', 'I normally dislike selective desaturation, but here it works; it has a purpose, and is integral to the concept. An intriguing image that holds my attention and cries out for repeated viewings.', '2010-09-05 12:37:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152491, 906756, 67258, '<td valign="top">We have a large gannet colony on the East coast of Yorkshire which I enjoy photographing - the North sea will never look as inviting as this turquoise sea though! I like the hint of the colony in the lower left, although do find the beak pointing up from the bottom a little distracting.</td>', 'We have a large gannet colony on the East coast of Yorkshire which I enjoy photographing - the North sea will never look as inviting as this turquoise sea though! I like the hint of the colony in the lower left, although do find the beak pointing up from the bottom a little distracting.', '2010-09-05 12:40:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152492, 906602, 67258, '<td valign="top">Superb detail, and thoroughly interesting.  You have done well to keep this arachnophobe''s attention!</td>', 'Superb detail, and thoroughly interesting.  You have done well to keep this arachnophobe''s attention!', '2010-09-05 12:41:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152493, 905603, 67258, '<td valign="top">Cute photo, but you have just missed the focus, which is a shame.</td>', 'Cute photo, but you have just missed the focus, which is a shame.', '2010-09-05 12:42:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152494, 906574, 67258, '<td valign="top">Not sure that the bridge and its reflection adds to the composition for me.  Like the lighting on your model though - lovely skin tones.</td>', 'Not sure that the bridge and its reflection adds to the composition for me.  Like the lighting on your model though - lovely skin tones.', '2010-09-05 12:44:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152495, 906428, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: A good degree of mystery in this image - her context and how you (as a photographer) relate to the scene produces a degree of intrigue. The catchlights in her glasses are excellent.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''m really not a fan of images that depict smoking but that aside, the skewed vertical knocks the image out of whack to me and your processing has served up a somewhat flat looking image. I think a bolder contrast profile might work a little better.<br/> <br/>Overall: Not one of my favourites but I respect the vision you had for this image.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: A good degree of mystery in this image - her context and how you (as a photographer) relate to the scene produces a degree of intrigue. The catchlights in her glasses are excellent. Critical stuff: I''m really not a fan of images that depict smoking but that aside, the skewed vertical knocks the image out of whack to me and your processing has served up a somewhat flat looking image. I think a bolder contrast profile might work a little better. Overall: Not one of my favourites but I respect the vision you had for this image.', '2010-09-05 12:45:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152496, 906750, 67258, '<td valign="top">Seriously disturbing; extraordinarily well done.  This creeps me out no end, but I am drawn back to it again and again.</td>', 'Seriously disturbing; extraordinarily well done.  This creeps me out no end, but I am drawn back to it again and again.', '2010-09-05 12:46:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152506, 906413, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I like unconventional portraits and this one fits the bill. Lovely lighting, both directionally and quality-wise. The ''pose'', if we can call it that (it looks too candid) contributes immensely to the mood of the image. Most of all though, I like the coloration - the red and green hues are wonderful and rich.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much - perhaps the image could take a tighter crop.<br/> <br/>Overall: Excellent work.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I like unconventional portraits and this one fits the bill. Lovely lighting, both directionally and quality-wise. The ''pose'', if we can call it that (it looks too candid) contributes immensely to the mood of the image. Most of all though, I like the coloration - the red and green hues are wonderful and rich. Critical stuff: Not much - perhaps the image could take a tighter crop. Overall: Excellent work.', '2010-09-05 13:15:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152508, 905712, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This an image with bags of appeal - the quality of the light and your choice of coloration make the building look as if it has been hewn from a block of gold. The figures almost look like placed toy figures (save for the motion blur), giving the image a stylised feel. I wonder about them and what kind of a day they were having.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing much.<br/> <br/>Overall: A fine and quirky image.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This an image with bags of appeal - the quality of the light and your choice of coloration make the building look as if it has been hewn from a block of gold. The figures almost look like placed toy figures (save for the motion blur), giving the image a stylised feel. I wonder about them and what kind of a day they were having. Critical stuff: Nothing much. Overall: A fine and quirky image.', '2010-09-05 13:23:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152518, 904744, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: A well used reflection indeed! I love the high key treatment with the intense red; the jiggledy mast juxtaposing with the straight orthogonal lines. The composition is perfect I feel, the placement of the subject and your crop are judged to perfection.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: A most pleasing image.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: A well used reflection indeed! I love the high key treatment with the intense red; the jiggledy mast juxtaposing with the straight orthogonal lines. The composition is perfect I feel, the placement of the subject and your crop are judged to perfection. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: A most pleasing image.', '2010-09-05 13:36:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152527, 904201, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: An excellent image which communicates the sense of foreboding your title suggests. The sense of two figures a foreground innocent and a middle distance demon is palpable - almost cinematic in its intensity. The focus on those concentric scratches (or is it a web) with all else cast into blurry (and desperate) ambiguity is the key to this image.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Hardly anything - the slight hints of cyan are a touch distracting, perhaps a pure monochrome edit would have looked a little cleaner.<br/> <br/>Overall: Visionary, inspired stuff.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: An excellent image which communicates the sense of foreboding your title suggests. The sense of two figures a foreground innocent and a middle distance demon is palpable - almost cinematic in its intensity. The focus on those concentric scratches (or is it a web) with all else cast into blurry (and desperate) ambiguity is the key to this image. Critical stuff: Hardly anything - the slight hints of cyan are a touch distracting, perhaps a pure monochrome edit would have looked a little cleaner. Overall: Visionary, inspired stuff.', '2010-09-05 13:43:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6152538, 902167, 57447, '<td valign="top">Captivating.</td>', 'Captivating.', '2010-09-05 14:18:22.000000', NULL, 1),
