(6153311, 903591, 115814, '<td valign="top">Not a member [yet...] so I can''t vote. Instead I''m clicking through the images and commenting on those that make me stop and look. This is one of those images.<br/> <br/>I''m guessing this might be Bodie, or some similar ghost town. The arrangement of the room and its contents feels staged. Nonetheless, this is a stunning photo. Highly effective use of wide angle, the B&amp;W processing is impeccable, and it tells a story I want to know more about. Kudos. Hope it does well...</td>', 'Not a member [yet...] so I can''t vote. Instead I''m clicking through the images and commenting on those that make me stop and look. This is one of those images. I''m guessing this might be Bodie, or some similar ghost town. The arrangement of the room and its contents feels staged. Nonetheless, this is a stunning photo. Highly effective use of wide angle, the B&W processing is impeccable, and it tells a story I want to know more about. Kudos. Hope it does well...', '2010-09-06 10:01:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6153316, 901401, 115814, '<td valign="top">Not a member [yet...] so I can''t vote. Instead I''m clicking through the images and commenting on those that make me stop and look. This is one of those images.<br/> <br/>I''m dying to come back after voting and see more about your processing. Its an effective homage to Norman Rockwell. Kudos. Hope it does well.</td>', 'Not a member [yet...] so I can''t vote. Instead I''m clicking through the images and commenting on those that make me stop and look. This is one of those images. I''m dying to come back after voting and see more about your processing. Its an effective homage to Norman Rockwell. Kudos. Hope it does well.', '2010-09-06 10:04:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6153317, 905091, 115814, '<td valign="top">Not a member [yet...] so I can''t vote. Instead I''m clicking through the images and commenting on those that make me stop and look. This is one of those images.<br/> <br/>Love the composition and the colors. This is a photo, I''ll come back to after the voting to get more info and look further at your portfolio. Kudos. Hope it does well.</td>', 'Not a member [yet...] so I can''t vote. Instead I''m clicking through the images and commenting on those that make me stop and look. This is one of those images. Love the composition and the colors. This is a photo, I''ll come back to after the voting to get more info and look further at your portfolio. Kudos. Hope it does well.', '2010-09-06 10:06:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6153322, 906582, 115814, '<td valign="top">Not a member [yet...] so I can''t vote. Instead I''m clicking through the images and commenting on those that make me stop and look. This is one of those images.<br/> <br/>Absolutely lovely. I''m having trouble identifying why this photo made me stop and look. Other than to say it''s an excellent take on a often attempted subject type. The placement of your horizon and composition that places more detail in the reflection than the sky is particularly effective, as is the limited presence of reds from the sky. Kudos. Hope it does well.</td>', 'Not a member [yet...] so I can''t vote. Instead I''m clicking through the images and commenting on those that make me stop and look. This is one of those images. Absolutely lovely. I''m having trouble identifying why this photo made me stop and look. Other than to say it''s an excellent take on a often attempted subject type. The placement of your horizon and composition that places more detail in the reflection than the sky is particularly effective, as is the limited presence of reds from the sky. Kudos. Hope it does well.', '2010-09-06 10:14:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6153324, 906695, 115814, '<td valign="top">Not a member [yet...] so I can''t vote. Instead I''m clicking through the images and commenting on those that make me stop and look. This is one of those images.<br/> <br/>I''ve seen this image (or ones like it) often - even tried to take a few. None in recent memory captures the scene as effectively as this. I particularly like the rugs on the green building. Kudos on a fine composition, spot on exposure, and sharpness and for not over-saturating the colors.</td>', 'Not a member [yet...] so I can''t vote. Instead I''m clicking through the images and commenting on those that make me stop and look. This is one of those images. I''ve seen this image (or ones like it) often - even tried to take a few. None in recent memory captures the scene as effectively as this. I particularly like the rugs on the green building. Kudos on a fine composition, spot on exposure, and sharpness and for not over-saturating the colors.', '2010-09-06 10:14:43.000000', NULL, 1),
