(6155556, 906829, 5585, '<td valign="top">There ya go Denis... a Free Study Blue...what''s it like up there in the rarefied air ? congrats and keep it up.</td>', 'There ya go Denis... a Free Study Blue...what''s it like up there in the rarefied air ? congrats and keep it up.', '2010-09-08 01:07:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(6155567, 902167, 99710, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by paulbtlw:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I knew I''d seen this image before - it stuck in my mind (I remembered her bare feet in the mud) and I checked back on 1x and there it was. It is truly great work though, the figure, the scene, the depth you have preserved - all the way back to the background wreckage; all make for a fantastic, sensitive, thought provoking piece. I also like the way she is walking towards a dark place in your image, reinforcing the metaphor in your title with photographic luminosity.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: I expect to see this on the front page. An easy 10 from me to help it on its way. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Paul for this wonderful comment.</td>', 'Originally posted by paulbtlw: I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I knew I''d seen this image before - it stuck in my mind (I remembered her bare feet in the mud) and I checked back on 1x and there it was. It is truly great work though, the figure, the scene, the depth you have preserved - all the way back to the background wreckage; all make for a fantastic, sensitive, thought provoking piece. I also like the way she is walking towards a dark place in your image, reinforcing the metaphor in your title with photographic luminosity. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: I expect to see this on the front page. An easy 10 from me to help it on its way.   Thanks Paul for this wonderful comment.', '2010-09-08 01:11:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(6155571, 902167, 99710, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Abra:</b></div><hr/><i> Of the 166 shots I''ve voted on so far this is by the far the best I''ve seen. Interesting lighting, works very well in B&amp;W, but the reason I''ve Faved this is because of the emotion and stories this gives me.  Well done! 10 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you very much!</td>', 'Originally posted by Abra: Of the 166 shots I''ve voted on so far this is by the far the best I''ve seen. Interesting lighting, works very well in B&W, but the reason I''ve Faved this is because of the emotion and stories this gives me.  Well done! 10   Thank you very much!', '2010-09-08 01:12:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(6155572, 906829, 67697, '<td valign="top">This was my top pick so I''m glad to see you won the blue.  Congrats!</td>', 'This was my top pick so I''m glad to see you won the blue.  Congrats!', '2010-09-08 01:12:20.000000', NULL, 0),
